  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing service delivery of community-based drug use prevention, treatment and care for people with drug use disorders toward innovative recovery in Lao People&apos;s Democratic Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed joint project aims to enhance the service delivery of community-based drug use prevention, treatment and care for people with drug use disorders toward innovative recovery (rehabilitation and social reintegration) by making the most use of the expertise of UNODC and UNIDO and complementing each other. UNIDO will be in charge of Component/Output 3: Skills and vocational training provided with target beneficiaries (= people with drug use disorders to be treated in Outputs 1 and 2/UNODC&apos;s components) to create income-generating opportunities in partnership with the private sector and TVET centers.</narrative>
  </description>
